  "notes": [
    "**Llevar** is a regular **-AR verb**",
    "No spelling changes or stem changes",
    "Past participle: **llevado** (regular)",
    "Multiple meanings:",
    "To carry: *llevar una maleta* (to carry a suitcase)",
    "To take (someone/something somewhere): *llevar a los niños al parque* (to take the kids to the park)",
    "To wear: *llevar gafas* (to wear glasses)",
    "To have been (time): *Llevo tres años aquí* (I've been here for three years)",
    "Often used reflexively: **llevarse** (to take away, to get along)",
    "Common usage: *llevar puesto* (to be wearing), *llevarse bien* (to get along well)",
    "Contrast with **traer** (to bring)",
    "Related noun: **el llevador** (carrier - less common)"
  ],
